  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;LOUIS DANGEARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Louis Dangeard is a French geologist, oceanographer, and cleric who has made significant contributions to both fields and holds the position of diocesan bishop."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CAEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Caen is an esteemed institution where Louis Dangeard taught geology and oceanography, known for producing distinguished scholars."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF LYON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Lyon is the institution where Louis Dangeard pursued his undergraduate studies in Earth Sciences."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF BORDEAUX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Bordeaux is where Louis Dangeard earned his Ph.D. in Oceanography."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH ACADEMY OF SCIENCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"French Academy of Sciences is an institution dedicated to promoting scientific excellence and advancing knowledge, where Louis Dangeard was an active member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH NATIONAL OCEANOGRAPHIC INSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"French National Oceanographic Institute is an organization where Louis Dangeard served as the Director, overseeing major research projects."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIOCESE OF LYON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diocese of Lyon is the religious organization where Louis Dangeard served as a parish priest and later as the diocesan bishop."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGLISH CHANNEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"English Channel is a body of water where Dangeard's work on geology contributed to our understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAY OF BISCAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bay of Biscay is a location where Dangeard conducted research on marine sedimentation and its impact on coastal ecosystems."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Academia refers to the realm of academic institutions and scholarly pursuits where Louis Dangeard worked and made significant contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARTH SCIENCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Earth Sciences is the field of study that includes geology and oceanography, which Louis Dangeard specialized in."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Geology is the branch of Earth Sciences that focuses on the study of the Earth's physical structure and substance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OCEANOGRAPHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oceanography is the branch of Earth Sciences that focuses on the study of the Earth's oceans and their properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE SEDIMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marine Sedimentation is the study of sediments in the ocean, which Dangeard researched extensively."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COASTAL ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coastal Ecosystems are the environments along the coastlines, which Dangeard studied in relation to marine sedimentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERFAITH DIALOGUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interfaith Dialogue is the discussion and cooperation between people of different religious beliefs, which Dangeard promoted."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL STEWARDSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental Stewardship is the responsibility to care for the environment, which Dangeard emphasized in his episcopal ministry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF OCEANOGRAPHY AND THEOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Journal of Oceanography and Theology is the publication where a study on Dangeard's episcopal ministry was published."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHOLIC HERALD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catholic Herald is the publication that highlighted Dangeard's efforts in promoting interfaith dialogue and cooperation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH COAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"French Coast is the area where Dangeard's research projects, such as the 'Oceanographic Survey of the French Coast,' took place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIDES OF ACADEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tides of Academia is the title of the document that chronicles the life and legacy of Louis Dangeard."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATE 19TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Late 19th Century is the period when Louis Dangeard was born and began his academic career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY AGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early Age refers to the early stages of Dangeard's career when he was developing his interests in geology and oceanography."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FORMATIVE STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Formative Stages refer to the early development of the fields of geology and oceanography during Dangeard's career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEACHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Teaching is the activity that Dangeard engaged in as a professor and parish priest, imparting knowledge to students and the congregation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Research is the activity that Dangeard conducted throughout his career, contributing to the advancement of knowledge in geology and oceanography."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUBLICATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Publications are the written works that Dangeard produced, sharing his research and findings with the academic community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLABORATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collaborations are the partnerships Dangeard formed with other researchers and institutions, contributing to the field of oceanography."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE GEOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marine Geology is the study of the Earth's oceans and their geological features, which Dangeard specialized in."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGLISH CHANNEL GEOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"English Channel Geology is the specific area of study where Dangeard made significant contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAY OF BISCAY RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bay of Biscay Research is the specific area of study where Dangeard conducted extensive research on marine sedimentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERFAITH COOPERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interfaith Cooperation is the collaboration between different religious groups, which Dangeard facilitated in his episcopal role."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL ISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental Issues are the topics Dangeard addressed in his episcopal ministry, emphasizing environmental stewardship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental issues are the topic discussed in the article, indicating a focus on ecological concerns."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BISHOP LOUIS DANGEARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bishop Louis Dangeard is a person whose scientific credentials have earned him respect and admiration from leaders of other faiths, facilitating greater collaboration and understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEADERS OF OTHER FAITHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leaders of other faiths are religious figures who respect and admire Bishop Louis Dangeard due to his scientific credentials."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0331</data>
    </node>
